and rename `remoteCommitMessage`'s `hash string` param to `rev string`.

**5. `refs_push_test.go:348` — delete `assert.Equal(t, 1, fake.batchCallCount(), "exactly one OPF invocation for the whole flush")`.**
Batching is already pinned by `TestRewriteQueuedCheckpointRefsWithOPF_RewritesThenIsIdempotent` (`manual_commit_opf_rewrite_test.go:941`, same message). This test's subject is whether the gate runs at all, which the trailer assertion proves. Minor companion: `assert.False(t, pushDisabled)` at :380 can become `_` for the `pushDisabled` return, matching the neighbouring `TestPushQueuedCheckpointRefs_PolicyBlocked`.

**6. `refs_push_test.go:363-366` — trim the failure test's doc comment to its first sentence.**
"Unlike the pre-push path — which withholds silently … surfaced as an error with the refs left queued" is the fourth statement of the same contrast (gate doc :246-248, `PushQueuedCheckpointRefs` doc :435-437, call-site comment :448-453). Keep only: "…is the fail-closed half: when OPF is enabled but the rewrite cannot run, nothing may reach the remote." Same treatment for :330-331 in the success test — "Without the gate the 8-layer commits were pushed verbatim and untagged" is past-tense history the first sentence already covers.

